{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"31d2b8ebf1f69ba4ac66cb0b4080ed41f0ed5f232b522f159a0a11c2a0b67620","digest":{"component_or_area":"review-bot git snapshot fetch","key_entities":["src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py","src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py","src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py","_fetch_origin","http.lowSpeedLimit","http.lowSpeedTime","_GIT_TIMEOUT","_interprocess_lock","_fetch_lock_for","_git"],"problem_keywords":["git fetch stall","low speed timeout","throughput abort","subprocess timeout","hanging fetch"],"propositions":["A stalled git fetch (connection established but zero bytes transferred) currently hangs for 300s before aborting, caused by missing http.lowSpeedLimit/http.lowSpeedTime config in the git argv","Adding http.lowSpeedLimit=1000 B/s and http.lowSpeedTime=10s configuration to the git fetch command aborts low-throughput connections in ~10 seconds instead of 300 seconds","In-process retry of low-speed aborts on a bounded attempt budget allows transient stalls to self-heal within the same review instead of deferring to backfill passes","A genuinely slow but progressing fetch (2000+ B/s) must not be aborted by the throughput threshold, distinguishing throughput-keyed abort from wall-time-keyed abort"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787492997531419001,"uuid":"0b55e893-ae6b-4934-93c1-df8184765003"}